framework DecisionAudit

domain CanonicalVelocityToken:
  description "Root-cause analysis for GitHub Issue #7"

problem P1:
  "Why can project observe-velocity emit a non-null adoptable_velocity_token that project set --velocity rejects?"

step S1:
  evidence EV1:
    "Issue #7 reports the exact observed rate 7200/827 point_per_hour with adoptable token 7200/827p/1h, followed by PTDSL-007 when that token is supplied unchanged to project set"
    resource:
      url "https://github.com/mako10k/perttool/issues/7"
      label "Public reproduction and expected round trip"

step S2:
  evidence EV2:
    "velocityToken serializes the rate numerator through the generic exact Duration serializer, which emits a fraction token when the Rational has a non-terminating decimal expansion"
    resource:
      file "src/history/velocity-observation.ts"
      label "Observation token generator"

step S3:
  evidence EV3:
    "parseVelocity accepts only integer or decimal point and period components, so the generic fraction point token is outside the active Velocity grammar"
    resource:
      file "src/parser/document-parser.ts"
      label "Velocity parser"

step S4:
  evidence EV4:
    "The exact Duration parser and serializer already duplicate numeric recognition and normalization across parser and model layers, while Velocity has no shared parse and canonical display utility"
    resource:
      file "src/model/exact-duration-source.ts"
      label "Existing exact numeric utility"

step S5:
  premise PR1:
    "A parser may accept more exact spellings than the formatter emits, but every emitted canonical token must parse to the identical reduced Rational rate"

step S6:
  decision D1 based_on P1, EV1, EV2, EV3:
    "The root cause is a producer-consumer grammar split: observation uses generic fraction Duration display while Velocity parsing and project mutation use a narrower independent recognizer"

step S7:
  decision D2 based_on EV4, PR1, D1:
    "Introduce shared exact scalar parsing plus a Velocity source utility that parses compatible integer, decimal, and fraction components, computes one reduced rate, and emits one unambiguous canonical integer-points over integer-period token"

step S8:
  decision D3 based_on PR1, D2:
    "Canonical display maps a positive reduced rate n/d point_per_hour or point_per_day to np/dh or np/dd, so 7200/827p/1h, 0.5p/1h, and 1p/2h share the canonical 1p/2h form when semantically equal"

step S9:
  decision D4 based_on D2, D3:
    "Source-preserving mutations retain unrelated valid source bytes; explicit formatting and newly generated adoptable tokens use canonical display, and declared velocity is never adopted automatically"

step S10:
  decision D5 based_on D2, D3, D4:
    "Acceptance requires parse-canonicalize-parse Rational identity, hour and day coverage, zero and malformed rejection, the 827-second public CLI replay, project set acceptance, and unchanged Grammar 8, CLI Contract 9, schema, command, facade, authority, and persistence identities"

step S11:
  pending PD1:
    "Release selection, publication, Issue mutation, plan advance, and unrelated work remain separate boundaries"
